      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This paper presents an evaluation of the logistic and Cox regression models for a prospective study when the outcome is binary and is determined in all patients after a fixed period of time. The similarities and differences between the regression coefficients and test statistics are given for the two-sample case. Extension of results to the multivariate case and under product binomial sampling are discussed. The results are illustrated using data from a clinical trial designed to evaluate the effect of a lipid lowering drug on progression of coronary artery disease."},
